  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish that Monte Carlo or hybrid MC/MD methods can generate chemical SRO, ordering, and compositionally enriched clusters in closely related bcc refractory high-entropy alloys. They also identify, in HfNbTaTiZr itself, lattice distortion as a cause of suppressed electron/phonon propagation, and separately document B2-type ordering in a related refractory alloy. An expert could therefore propose using simulated SRO to reduce distortion and potentially increase thermal conductivity. However, none of the records connects SRO to thermal transport, identifies HfTi and TiZr clusters, predicts B2-like percolating high-conductivity pathways, or addresses the phonon-density-of-states changes. Those central mechanistic elements require a substantial additional insight, so the set points in the right direction without fully reconstructing the later result."
